# Git & PR Conventions

- Use Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`,
  `test:`, `ci:`. Scope optional, e.g. `feat(api): add get-document handler`.
- Keep commits small and focused; the message explains the why.
- All changes go through pull requests; CI (lint, typecheck, tests, terraform
  validate, Checkov) must be green before merge.
- Update `docs/features.md` acceptance criteria and add an ADR when a decision is
  made.
- Never commit secrets or `.env` files; never commit Terraform state.

```text
feat(api): generate presigned upload URL

Add create-upload-url handler that writes an UPLOADED record and returns a
short-lived presigned PUT URL. Implements HRM-001.
```
